"helpText" = "## How to use\n1. Open a page in Safari, Google Chrome, Firefox, Microsoft Edge or another supported browser.\n2. Press a function’s hotkey. LinkMaker reads the title and URL of the page and copies, saves or reopens it.\n3. The result appears briefly at the top of the screen and stays in “Last result” and at the top of the menu-bar menu.\n- Hotkeys are registered only while a target browser is in front; in other apps the same keys keep their own meaning.\n- Every function is also in the menu-bar link icon’s menu; it acts on the browser used last.\n\n## Palette\n- Open it with **⌃⌥⌘M** (in any app; press again to hide), Show Palette in the menu-bar menu, or Show Palette in the main window.\n- Each button runs its function on the page in the browser in front. The palette never takes the focus, so the browser stays in front. Hover a button to see its hotkey.\n- It hides while an excluded app is in front and returns with any other app. The “From selected text” buttons work in any app. After you close it, it stays closed until you call it again.\n- In Settings → Palette you can change its hotkey and show it instead of the main window at launch and on reopen.\n- Switch between Simple and Full with the menu at the top of the palette. Choose the Simple mode buttons in Settings → Palette (by default: Copy as…, URL only, Markdown, URLs only of all open tabs, Save as webloc…, Reload with a simple URL and Open in edit mode). Hidden functions still work from their hotkeys and the menu bar.\n- The menu next to it (or Settings → Palette) sets the button style for both Simple and Full: Icon and Text, Icon Only or Text Only. With icons only, hovering a button still shows its name and hotkey.\n\n## Functions and default hotkeys\n### Copy title and URL\n- **⌥C** Copy as…: shows the formats (URL only, text, Markdown, HTML, and the Amazon links on a product page) at the mouse pointer.\n- **⌥S** URL only · **⌥T** title, line break, URL · **⌥Y** title, space, URL\n- **⌥M** Markdown (- [title](URL)) · **⌥H** HTML (<a href=\"URL\">title</a>)\n- **⌥A** Amazon link (on a product page; https://www.amazon.co.jp/dp/ASIN)\n- **⌥A ×2** (double tap) Amazon link (Associates), using the Associate ID in Output\n- A single ⌥A runs after a short wait (about 0.3 s) for a second press. Any function can be set to “Double tap” in Settings → Hotkeys (one single and one double function per key).\n### All open tabs (Safari, Google Chrome, Firefox; front window. Firefox reads its saved session: tabs opened in the last 15 seconds or so may be missing, and private windows are not supported)\n- **⌥G** Copy as…: a menu of formats (URLs only, with titles, Markdown) at the mouse pointer\n- **⌃⌥⇧⌘W** Close Other Tabs: closes every tab of the front window except the current one (pinned tabs stay; Firefox needs the Accessibility permission)\n### Save as a file\n- **⌥W** Save as webloc… and **⌥Q** Save QR code (PNG)… ask where at the mouse pointer: Desktop, each open Finder / Path Finder window (by folder name, front first), Recent Folders (Finder and Path Finder history), or Choose Folder….\n- Files are named after the page title (“qr-title” for QR codes). Existing files are never replaced; “ 2” etc. is added.\n- QR codes are made on this Mac; nothing is sent to an online QR service.\n### Reopen\n- **⌥R** reload with a simple URL · **⌥⇧⌘R** force reload\n- **⌥⌘E** open in edit mode (note article → editor, Tally form → edit, Doorkeeper event → management)\n- **⌥⇧⌘T** open in Google Translate (new tab) · **⌃⌘N** new window (closes the original tab) · **⌥⇧⌘P** private window\n### Open in another browser\n- **⌥⇧⌘S** Safari, **⌥⇧⌘G** Google Chrome, **⌥⇧⌘F** Firefox, **⌥⇧⌘E** Microsoft Edge, **⌥⇧⌘N** Notion (a Notion page in the Notion app)\n### From the clipboard\n- **⌃⌥⌘L** open URLs on the clipboard · search each copied line in its own tab (no default key). Up to 30 at a time.\n\n### From selected text (any app except excluded ones)\nSelect text and press the key: LinkMaker copies it (⌘C) and reads it. With no selection, the clipboard text is used. The previous clipboard is put back afterwards.\n- **⌥⌘L** open URLs in the default browser · **⌃⌘L** choose a browser · **⌥⇧⌘L** open in Safari, Firefox and Chrome\n- Excluded apps (defaults: Illustrator, InDesign, Photoshop, Word) never get these keys; edit the list in Settings → Excluded Apps.\n- ⌥⌘L is also Downloads in Safari and Chrome; change the key if you need that.\n\n## How URLs and titles are cleaned\n- Amazon URLs become https://www.amazon.co.jp/dp/ASIN.\n- Tracking parameters (utm_…, fbclid, gclid…) and a trailing index.html are removed.\n- “Remove the query” (on by default) drops everything after “?” except on Google, YouTube and URLs with “id=”.\n- Unread counts such as “(3) ” and browser names in window titles are removed. New tabs and start pages are ignored.\n\n## Settings\n- Startup & Background: launch at login (off by default), hide main window at startup, hide from Dock and App Switcher (keeps the app out of the Dock and ⌘Tab; show it from the menu-bar icon or by opening it again in Finder), keep running, menu-bar icon, Accessibility and Automation, restart and quit.\n- Hotkeys: pause (until relaunch), each function on/off and double tap. Click Change…, then press the keys (include ⌘, ⌥ or ⌃; standard keys such as ⌘C and keys used by another function with the same tap count or by the palette are refused; Esc cancels). Reset to Default restores the default key unless another one uses it, and Clear removes it.\n- Browsers: each browser on/off (all on by default).\n- Output: URL cleanup, Amazon Associate ID, translation language, success messages.\n- About: version and links. Open Settings with ⌘, and close with ⌘W.\n\n## Sharing settings\n- In Settings > Sharing, share each function’s hotkey, on/off and double tap, the palette hotkey, palette mode and simple-mode buttons, the browsers and the output settings (URL cleanup, Associate ID, translation language, result display) with your other Macs.\n- **Export & Import**: “Export…” writes LinkMaker-Settings.plist; on another Mac, choose that file with “Import…”; this Mac’s settings are replaced with the file’s. Cancel changes nothing.\n- **Settings Sync**: click “Set Sync Folder…” and choose a folder in iCloud Drive, Dropbox or similar. Choose the same folder on your other Macs to keep changes in step automatically. With a sync service, keep this folder downloaded and available offline.\n- Login launch, background, menu bar, Accessibility, window positions, excluded apps and export folders stay per Mac.\n\n## Permissions\n- Accessibility (required): reads the page title and URL and sends keys such as typing in the address bar. Turn on LinkMaker in System Settings → Privacy & Security → Accessibility.\n- Automation (some functions): “All open tabs” asks the browser and “Save as webloc…” and “Save QR code (PNG)…” ask Finder and Path Finder. Choose OK the first time.\n\n## The clipboard\n- Reopen functions paste the URL into the address bar, using the clipboard briefly and restoring it afterwards — unless something else was copied in the meantime.\n\n## Running and quitting\n- The menu-bar link icon offers every function, the main window, Settings, Pause, Help and Quit. Hide the icon with “Menu Bar Settings…” in the app menu.\n- Closing windows keeps the app running; open it again from the Dock or Finder to show the main window.\n- Quit with “Quit LinkMaker” or ⌘Q while the app is in front.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n- Nothing happens: check that the browser and the function are on and that hotkeys are not paused.\n- “Could not read the page URL”: wait for the page to load and try again.\n- While ⌥+letter hotkeys are registered, those characters (ß etc.) cannot be typed in the browser. Change or turn off the key.\n- Shown as not allowed after allowing: relaunch. If that does not help, remove LinkMaker from the list in System Settings and add it again.\n\n## Privacy\nNo network communication (update checks stay off until a feed is configured). URLs, titles and clipboard contents are not recorded or sent.\n\n## Uninstall\nDelete LinkMaker from Applications. To remove settings, delete ~/Library/Preferences/jp.dtp-transit.linkmaker.plist and remove the app from Login Items, Accessibility and Automation.";
